  "body": "Stacked on #1144 (on #1139, #1123, #560, #551). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nExpected merges: #539 (tabs) and #540 (no-core) are worked on the same base and will likely touch `WireContourOp`, `WireParams`, the DTO and `wire_page.rs` - both sides add fields, keep both. #1147 / #1150 are stacked nearby.\n\n## What changed\n\nA constant wire taper (#290 D2, D5, D7), as the move pose:\n\n- **Op**: `WireContourOp.taper_deg` (signed degrees; 0 = vertical, positive widens the profile downward from the top plane). The DTO omits it at 0, the stamp digests it only when non-zero, so every existing file, stamp, CL and NC is unchanged. The Geometry tab has a Taper angle field.\n- **Generator** (`motion::wire_edm::taper`): the profile and every #532 law are held on the top plane at the kerf measured across the leaning wire (`k / cos a`). Each lower-plane vertex is moved `H tan a` along the mitre, so each side's face is planar at exactly the angle. Each move's pose is the wire's direction toward the upper guide. The wire stands upright at the start hole. Refused by name: no `edm.max_taper_deg`, an angle (or a corner's lean) above it (naming the op and the angle), a side the lean folds over, a corner too sharp to lean.\n- **Verify** (`sim::verify::wire`): `WireJob.taper` lifts #534's posed-move refusal only for a cut that states a taper. At every judged height the wire's section is `to + t (z - z0)`. The kerf's reach toward the product is `k sqrt(1 + (t.u)^2)` (the leaning kerf's elliptical section). The slug is judged per height. So a gouge at any height blocks the post.\n- **Machine check** (`machine::wire_edm`): every pose is judged against the max taper, the guide planes (`edm.lower_guide_z` / `upper_guide_z`, which must hold the programmed plane), and the U/V offset against the U and V strokes. Missing guide planes or a missing U/V axis are refused by name. The lower guide's X/Y is also checked against X/Y travel.\n- **Post**: `posting_wire` turns each leaning move into the lower guide's X Y plus `PARAM WireU`/`WireV` (the upper guide's offset), computed from the pose and the guide planes. `wire-iso.cps` writes `edm.codes.taper_on` before the first leaning move, `uv` (a template with `{u}` `{v}`) on each one, and `taper_off` once the wire is upright, before the wire cut. A missing code refuses by name. The angle-word form is not offered (see the decision record).\n- Fixture `wire-iso-fixture.mch` now states guide planes, a 15 degree maximum, U/V strokes and synthetic taper codes. `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md` lists the new params. The decision record is `docs/decisions/536-wire-taper.md`.\n\n## Sources\n\nPlane trigonometry only (the section of a leaning cylinder, the polygon mitre) over #290's D2/D5/D7. ISO 6983 U/V as secondary axes parallel to X/Y. No vendor material.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/wire_taper.rs` (new):\n  - `a_tapered_punch_posts_its_golden_and_its_cl_shows_the_poses`: goldens `tests/golden/nc/wire-iso/wire_taper_punch.nc` and `tests/golden/wire_taper_punch.cl`; the wire laws are clean.\n  - `a_zero_taper_is_the_vertical_golden_byte_for_byte`: checked against the existing `wire_contour_punch.nc`, on the extended fixture.\n  - `a_taper_past_the_machines_maximum_is_refused_by_name`: 30 degrees on a 15 degree machine, plus an unstated maximum.\n  - `a_uv_offset_past_the_stroke_or_the_guides_is_refused_by_name`: U stroke, guides' reach, no U axis, no guide planes.\n  - `a_taper_whose_lower_edge_gouges_the_part_blocks_the_post`\n- `motion` unit test `a_taper_leans_every_side_by_its_angle_and_zero_is_the_vertical_cut`\n- The existing wire suites (wire_post, wire_verify, wire_contour, golden_cl, sim wire tests), the quick gate and clippy `-D warnings` on motion/sim/app/ui: clean. `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/534-wire-verify` on the final head e34cf882: sim, motion, app (incl. wire_taper, wire_post, wire_verify, wire_contour, golden_cl, edm_*) and ui suites all ok (12.1 min, 0 failed).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Not run on a real EDM control (D10). The fixture's taper codes are invented.\n- Angle-word taper dialects and arcs under taper (refused).\n- A die with sharp inside corners under taper: the corner law refuses it as for a vertical cut.\n- No snapshot PNGs changed.\n\nMCP: the Wire Contour's DTO carries `taper_deg` (optional), so the existing op tools take it with no new command.\n\nChangelog: Wire EDM: constant taper on the Wire Contour - posed moves, leaning-kerf verification at every height, max-angle / guide / U-V stroke refusals, and UV taper words from the machine's edm.codes (#536)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #536\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
